WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:15.135
Every morning was eventful at the March home, today being no different.

2
00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:18.558
Amy had overslept and was very cranky.

3
00:00:18.559 --> 00:00:23.379
Her hair, her most precious asset, looked limp and lifeless.

4
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.525
"May I please be excused from school?

5
00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:36.296
I'm just not happy today," she whined, munching on a piece of dry bread that would have been warm and soft if she had gotten up in time to eat it.

6
00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:39.072
"Well, then we should all stay home.

7
00:00:39.073 --> 00:00:44.311
I'm not happy and neither is Meg," Jo shouted sarcastically from the foyer.

8
00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:48.765
Late as usual, the two older girls were hastening to get out the door,

9
00:00:48.766 --> 00:00:54.401
but Jo couldn't find The Pirate's Enigma, a book she had borrowed from Aunt March.

10
00:00:54.402 --> 00:01:00.214
"Where could that stupid book be?" Jo yelled in frustration.

11
00:01:00.215 --> 00:01:03.611
"Jo! Mind your tongue and mind your temper!"

12
00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:07.348
Mother rebuked as she yanked at Amy's knots.

13
00:01:07.349 --> 00:01:11.734
"I'll look for the book," Beth offered in her timid manner.

14
00:01:11.735 --> 00:01:17.150
"Pray for me that Aunt March won't have an urge to hear that story read to her today.

15
00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:27.978
I'll just pretend to be deaf or have a sore throat if she does," Jo remarked, shoving her arms into her thick coat, and finally stepping outside the door.

16
00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:32.917
Blowing kisses at everyone, Meg and Jo began their trek to work.

17
00:01:32.918 --> 00:01:36.132
When Mother went to the window to wave at her girls,

18
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:43.104
Amy reluctantly gathered her school books, got her lunch pail from Hannah, and dragged her feet to the foyer.

19
00:01:43.105 --> 00:01:49.100
"You're so lucky you can stay home all day," Amy said wistfully to Beth.

20
00:01:49.101 --> 00:01:53.298
At other times when Amy said this Beth would shake her head and say,

21
00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:57.820
"You're the lucky one. I wish I could go to school."

22
00:01:57.821 --> 00:02:05.364
Today, however, Beth did not say anything because inside she was feeling very lucky.

23
00:02:05.365 --> 00:02:10.011
Today she had something very special to look forward to.

24
00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:18.466
It seemed to take an eternity before everyone was finally gone. Beth was all by herself.

25
00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:27.827
The kitchen door of the March home faced the Laurence mansion, in particular the conservatory, where the object of Beth's desire was.

26
00:02:27.828 --> 00:02:34.167
Beth, however, had a major obstacle to overcome first: her fear.

27
00:02:34.168 --> 00:02:40.673
"What if Mr. Laurence suddenly walks into the conservatory?" she said to herself.

28
00:02:40.674 --> 00:02:44.981
"What if Laurie hears me play and thinks I'm horrible.

29
00:02:44.982 --> 00:02:53.473
Then what if he tells Jo? What if the door locks after I'm inside and I can't get out?"

30
00:02:53.474 --> 00:03:01.883
But no matter how many "what ifs" Beth could think of, her fear did not hold her back from the beautiful instrument inside.

31
00:03:01.884 --> 00:03:05.582
Taking a deep breath, she opened the kitchen door.

32
00:03:05.583 --> 00:03:12.581
Sticking her head out and checking to make sure no one was around, she took one brave step forward.

33
00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:19.832
Then, like a frightened field mouse, she scurried across the yard onto the stone pathway that led to the mansion.

34
00:03:19.833 --> 00:03:27.035
Pausing to cool her flushed cheeks, Beth felt like an intruder, as if she were entering a home not her own.

35
00:03:27.036 --> 00:03:36.233
Mr. Laurence, of course, had given his permission; yet, it was an odd sensation as Beth pushed open the glass doors to the conservatory.

36
00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:47.269
As Mr. Laurence had promised, the room was empty, and as before Beth caught her breath when her gaze fell upon the beautiful piano.

37
00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:55.108
"Hello. I'm Beth." The magnificence of the musical instrument impelled her to introduce herself.

38
00:03:55.109 --> 00:04:02.769
Giggling, she continued, "Mr. Laurence says I must come every day and look after you."

39
00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:10.987
She lightly stroked the keys. "He doesn't want you to get dusty or for your keys to get stuck."

40
00:04:10.988 --> 00:04:18.504
Even with Beth's amateur touch, she knew none of the polished keys ever got stuck.

41
00:04:18.505 --> 00:04:24.942
"But just between you and me," she leaned closer to the piano, as if she were whispering a secret,

42
00:04:24.943 --> 00:04:29.568
"I was hoping he would ask so I could come and play music on you."

43
00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:35.318
Pulling the stool out, Beth carefully sat down on the soft velvet cushion.

44
00:04:35.319 --> 00:04:41.918
"Oh, look!" Beth reached out to open an old leather book resting on the stand.

45
00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:47.707
Inside was a collection of sheet music, many of them songs that Beth knew.

46
00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:53.099
"You even prepared music for me to play. How kind you are!"

47
00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.997
Beth lovingly patted the top of the piano.

48
00:04:57.998 --> 00:05:06.326
After taking a moment to select a song, Beth clenched and unclenched her fists, as she'd seen pianists do.

49
00:05:06.327 --> 00:05:10.457
Then, ever so cautiously, she began to play.

50
00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:16.998
At first, the sounds were timid, like Beth, and unsure, lacking confidence and power.

51
00:05:16.999 --> 00:05:25.512
However, as she practiced and became more acquainted with her new friend, she felt comfortable enough to open her soul.

52
00:05:25.513 --> 00:05:31.777
Oblivious to the passing of time, Beth fell into a world of sound and harmony.

53
00:05:31.778 --> 00:05:36.679
True to her word, Beth visited the conservatory every day.

54
00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:43.602
Even though Hannah scolded her for not eating properly or practicing so long that her bones were stiff and numb,

55
00:05:43.603 --> 00:05:49.290
Beth felt that nothing could give her greater happiness than the time she spent playing music.

56
00:05:49.291 --> 00:05:58.007
Unknown to Beth, she already had a couple of secret admirers who also were finding joy and comfort in her melodies.

57
00:05:58.008 --> 00:06:06.597
One of them should have been paying closer attention to his lessons, but found himself straining his ears to hear Beth's music.

58
00:06:06.598 --> 00:06:10.702
After Laurie discovered he could hear Beth playing downstairs,

59
00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:16.130
he deliberately opened a window in the library in order to hear the music more clearly.

60
00:06:16.131 --> 00:06:23.089
"Must you keep that window open? It's freezing in here," Mr. Brookes complained to his young pupil.

61
00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:28.585
Mr. Brookes was not amused since the temperature outside was way below zero.

62
00:06:28.586 --> 00:06:33.834
The other admirer chose to sit in his study, lean back in his chair,

63
00:06:33.835 --> 00:06:41.894
and remember the time when his own little girl's music could be heard through those very walls.

64
00:06:41.895 --> 00:06:48.524
Since everyone was home on the weekends, Beth could not practice her beloved piano in the conservatory,

65
00:06:48.525 --> 00:06:53.416
but she continued to play the music in her mind wherever she was.

66
00:06:53.417 --> 00:06:57.099
One Saturday, after returning from the grocer's with Hannah,

67
00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:03.022
Beth found herself encircled by her sisters, all of them shouting with excitement at once.

68
00:07:03.023 --> 00:07:06.601
"You've got a gift, Beth!" screamed Amy.

69
00:07:06.602 --> 00:07:10.107
"A gift?" Beth asked, confused.

70
00:07:10.108 --> 00:07:16.453
"Come see it. Come!" Jo took Beth's arm and led her to the living room.

71
00:07:16.454 --> 00:07:23.871
As she stepped into the familiar room, Beth's eyes immediately went to the corner where something new stood.

72
00:07:23.872 --> 00:07:27.960
It was a beautiful solid oak piano.

73
00:07:27.961 --> 00:07:34.221
"Is this really for me?" she whispered, her voice trembling.

74
00:07:34.222 --> 00:07:39.373
"Look at this card, Beth!" Jo swung a white envelope in her face.

75
00:07:39.374 --> 00:07:42.926
"Read it! Hurry, Beth!" Amy pleaded.

76
00:07:42.927 --> 00:07:49.750
"I can't. I'm too nervous. Jo, can you read it for me, please?" asked Beth.

77
00:07:49.751 --> 00:07:54.709
Jo ripped the envelope open and read in a loud voice.

78
00:07:54.710 --> 00:08:01.517
My dearest Beth, I'm afraid you may not like what I am about to say.

79
00:08:01.518 --> 00:08:07.135
But I must confess that I have been listening to your beautiful music from my study.

80
00:08:07.136 --> 00:08:13.933
You may not realize it but your lovely melodies have brought much happiness back into my home.

81
00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:23.222
Therefore, as a token of my deepest appreciation, please accept this gift, which, at one time, belonged to my own daughter.

82
00:08:23.223 --> 00:08:28.713
May it bring much music and joy to your home and hearts, as it has done to mine.

83
00:08:28.714 --> 00:08:35.375
Your greatest admirer, Mr. Laurence
